 "reading": "Neither acquisition-time pair support nor temporal-edge density explains the 16-tag level. The three equal-size blocks differ in fitted offset by at most **0.0385** (**0.4200** / **0.4065** / **0.3815**), which is **0.39** to **1.68** standard errors of the pairwise difference at six seeds each and no wider than the within-block seed spread (**0.043** / **0.073** / **0.036**). Pair support barely moves \u2014 mean **22.90** / **22.61** / **22.62**, median **22.33** / **22.00** / **21.50**, mass **1458** / **1443** / **1444**, dispersion **7.88** / **7.77** / **8.14**, share at support <= 10 **0.045** / **0.034** / **0.029** \u2014 and temporal-edge density does not move at all: **176.0** / **176.0** / **175.8** distinct temporal edges, **11.00** / **11.00** / **10.99** per tag, so a quantity the two-tags-per-event law pins at **11** edges per tag cannot carry a level that varies. Of **11** quantities, **4** order the three block means the way the level does \u2014 median support, tag entropy, the support <= 10 share and the temporal-edge share (**2.765** / **2.757** / **2.755**) \u2014 each a one-in-six chance ordering, and none keeps a consistent sign at seed resolution: median support runs **-0.62** / **+0.38** / **-0.09**, tag entropy **-0.77** / **+0.14** / **-0.46**, the floor share **+0.14** / **-0.60** / **-0.82** and the edge share **+0.21** / **-0.65** / **+0.69**. The sharpest single case against a support account is fresh-16's lowest seed, `20650105` at offset **+0.2589**, which has that block's **highest** mean support (**23.0**). The lowest block matches fresh-16 on candidate count (**63.8** against **63.8**), K completeness (**1.000**) and temporal-edge density (**11.00** against **10.99**), so the level is not carried by candidate support, support mass, support dispersion, entropy, cell-pair coverage, pair saturation or the size of the temporal graph: it varies more inside a block than between equal-size blocks, and the fitted block offset is a mean of draws rather than a property of the candidate space.",
